## Key Takeaways

- Always scan **all ports** (`-p-`), not just common ones — SSH was hidden on 2222
- Directory enumeration is essential — the vulnerable CMS was only reachable via `/simple`
- Outdated CMS versions are frequently vulnerable to well-documented CVEs
- `sudo -l` is one of the first commands to run after gaining initial access
- Giving a user sudo access to a text editor like `vim` is equivalent to giving them a root shell — avoid this in production environments
